  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The empirical comparison is limited to park access metrics evaluated within two cities.",
      "what": "Evaluating OpenStreetMap, Esri, SafeGraph, and The Trust for Public Land across two cities reveals significant discrepancies in measured park access. These variations stem directly from differences in feature completeness, spatial coverage, and attribute accuracy among the four geospatial sources.",
      "why": "Urban planning decisions and equity evaluations relying on park accessibility metrics can yield contradictory outcomes simply based on the underlying data provider chosen."
